{{!-- The Rote list, on the Stats tab, in the band under Arete and Health.

      It used to render on the Powers tab through `powerSections` (`assets/data/sheet/powertab.js`,
      the mage `primary` list) with the two-column "column" layout. It moved here for the same
      reason the Spheres did: a mage casts from Spheres and Rotes, both are now one click from the
      sheet's first page, and clicking either opens the same casting screen.

      `rotes` comes from `addRoteContext`, which `prepareStatContext` calls — an ApplicationV2 part
      only carries the context its OWN preparer built, so moving the include without moving the
      context renders an empty block and nothing says so.

      `power_listpower.hbs` is reused verbatim rather than reimplemented: it is what the Powers tab
      rendered, so a Rote row looks and behaves exactly as it did, click-to-cast included. --}}
<div class="sheet-area flex-columns">

	<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont" data-area="rotes">
		<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize "wod.spheres.rotes"}}</span>
	</div>

	<div class="item-column">
		{{#each rotes as |item id|}}
			<div>
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_listpower.hbs"
					item=item config=../config actor=../actor locked=../locked showclear=false}}
			</div>
		{{/each}}
	</div>

</div>
